# Security

How to report a vulnerability, and what happens next.

## Reporting a Vulnerability

Report it privately, through GitHub's [private vulnerability reporting][report],
never in a public issue. Say what is affected, how to reproduce it, and what it
lets an attacker do.

The report is acknowledged within a week. A fix, where there is one, is released
with an advisory that credits the reporter, unless they ask otherwise.

## Supported Versions

The newest release is supported: a fix is released as a new version, not
backported.

[report]: https://github.com/atomix-labs/devset/security/advisories/new
